<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="tour-detail-layout">
  <div class="tour-detail-main reveal">
    <h2>Tour Overview</h2>
    <p>This extraordinary 19-day journey spans two of the Silk Road's most fascinating regions — China's wild Xinjiang province and the legendary cities of Uzbekistan. Begin in Kashgar, China's westernmost city, traverse the Karakoram Highway, explore the Mogao Caves, then fly to Tashkent to discover the turquoise domes of Samarkand, the ancient streets of Bukhara, and the desert citadel of Khiva. This is the ultimate Silk Road experience.</p>

    <div class="highlight-box"><h3>Trip Highlights</h3><ul>
      <li>Drive the legendary Karakoram Highway to Taxkorgan</li><li>Marvel at the Mogao Caves in Dunhuang</li><li>Stand in awe at Registan Square, Samarkand</li><li>Wander through Bukhara's UNESCO-listed Old City</li><li>Explore the ancient walled city of Khiva</li><li>Experience Kashgar's vibrant Sunday Market</li><li>Visit the Flaming Mountains and Grape Valley in Turpan</li><li>Ride the high-speed train from Samarkand to Bukhara</li>
    </ul></div>

    <h2>Day-by-Day Itinerary</h2>
    <ul class="itinerary">
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>1</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Arrive in Kashgar</h4><p>Welcome to Kashgar! Your guide meets you at the airport and transfers you to your hotel. Free evening to explore the Old City at your own pace.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Kashgar 4★</span><span>🍽 Dinner</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>2</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar — Sunday Market &amp; Old City</h4><p>Experience the legendary Sunday Market, a trading hub for over 2,000 years. Visit the Id Kah Mosque and explore the winding alleys of the Old City. Afternoon at Abakh Khoja Tomb.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Kashgar 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>3</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar — Karakoram Highway to Taxkorgan</h4><p>Journey along one of the world's highest paved roads. Stop at Karakul Lake (3,600m) with stunning views of Muztagh Ata (7,546m). Arrive in Taxkorgan, China's westernmost town.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Taxkorgan 3★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>4</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Taxkorgan → Kashgar</h4><p>Visit the ancient Stone Fort and grasslands. Return to Kashgar via the Karakoram Highway with photo stops at panoramic viewpoints.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Kashgar 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>5</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar → Kuqa (Train)</h4><p>Board the train to Kuqa, an ancient Silk Road oasis. Visit the Kizil Thousand Buddha Caves and the mysterious Tianshan Grand Canyon.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Kuqa 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>6</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kuqa → Urumqi (Flight)</h4><p>Morning flight to Urumqi. Visit the Xinjiang Regional Museum to see the famous Tarim mummies. Afternoon at Hongshan Park for panoramic city views.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Urumqi 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>7</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Urumqi → Turpan</h4><p>Drive to Turpan, the second-lowest depression on Earth. Visit the Jiaohe Ancient Ruins and the ingenious Karez underground irrigation system.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Turpan 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>8</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Turpan → Dunhuang (High-Speed Train)</h4><p>Morning visit to the Flaming Mountains and Grape Valley. Afternoon high-speed train to Dunhuang.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Dunhuang 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>9</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang — Mogao Caves &amp; Singing Sand Dunes</h4><p>Full day at two UNESCO sites. Morning at Mogao Caves (8 caves). Afternoon camel ride at the Singing Sand Dunes and Crescent Moon Spring.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Dunhuang 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>10</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang ✈ Tashkent</h4><p>Fly to Tashkent via Urumqi. Upon arrival, transfer to hotel. Evening walk through Amir Timur Square.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Tashkent 4★</span><span>🍽 B/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>11</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Tashkent City Tour</h4><p>Explore Uzbekistan's modern capital. Visit Khast Imam Complex (home of the world's oldest Quran), Chorsu Bazaar, and the ornate Tashkent Metro stations.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Tashkent 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>12</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Tashkent → Samarkand (High-Speed Train)</h4><p>Take the Afrosiyob train to Samarkand. Visit Registan Square — one of the world's most magnificent architectural ensembles. Explore Gur-e-Amir Mausoleum and Bibi-Khanym Mosque.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Samarkand 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>13</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Samarkand — Shah-i-Zinda &amp; Silk Paper Workshop</h4><p>Visit the necropolis of Shah-i-Zinda, Ulugh Beg Observatory, and a traditional silk paper workshop. Afternoon free to explore Siab Bazaar.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Samarkand 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>14</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Samarkand → Bukhara (High-Speed Train)</h4><p>Train to the holy city of Bukhara. Walk through the atmospheric Old City. Visit Lyab-i Hauz plaza, the Ark Citadel, and the Kalon Minaret.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Bukhara 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>15</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Bukhara — Full Day Exploration</h4><p>Discover Bukhara's 140+ architectural monuments. Visit the Samanid Mausoleum, Chor Minor, and a traditional hammam. Evening folk show with dinner.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Bukhara 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>16</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Bukhara → Khiva (Drive through Kyzylkum Desert)</h4><p>Scenic drive across the Kyzylkum Desert to the ancient walled city of Khiva. Arrive in the afternoon and explore Ichan-Kala, the UNESCO-listed inner city.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Khiva 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>17</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Khiva — Full Day in the Open-Air Museum</h4><p>Full day exploring Khiva's perfectly preserved medieval architecture. Visit the Kalta Minor Minaret, Juma Mosque with its 213 wooden columns, and the Tash-Hauli Palace.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Khiva 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>18</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Khiva → Tashkent (Flight)</h4><p>Morning flight back to Tashkent. Free afternoon for last-minute shopping at Chorsu Bazaar. Farewell dinner at a traditional Uzbek restaurant.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Tashkent 4★</span><span>🍽 B/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>19</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Depart Tashkent</h4><p>Transfer to Tashkent International Airport. Your epic Silk Road journey concludes. Safe travels!</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🍽 B</span></div></div></li>
    </ul>

